//! XKB keysym name table and lookup (kmscon grab parsing, ROADMAP M7.1).
//!
//! Generated from the libxkbcommon 1.13.2 `xkbcommon-keysyms.h` header
//! (nixpkgs pin); do not edit the tables by hand. The lookup replicates
//! `xkb_keysym_from_name()` semantics without linking xkbcommon:
//!
//!   * case-sensitive name lookup (binary search over `entries`),
//!   * `U+XXXX` Unicode notation (direct encoding above U+00FF, Latin-1
//!     normalization at or below it, exactly like xkbcommon),
//!   * `0x…` raw hexadecimal notation (no normalization),
//!   * the `XF86_` → `XF86` underscore-strip fallback.
//!
//! `fromNameIgnoreCase` mirrors `XKB_KEYSYM_CASE_INSENSITIVE`: among
//! case-insensitive duplicates the last one in (lowercased name, name)
//! order wins — xkbcommon's "best" (lower-case) variant. Grabs use it only
//! to produce the "did you mean …?" suggestion; keysyms are case-sensitive.

